Subject: register VM fills a frame's registers from a static `undefined` template

What this does:
  `regvm_record_fill` gives a callee frame its initial register values before the
  program runs. Two properties have to hold at once. Every register must hold a
  valid, *not reference counted* word, because the store handlers release the
  destination's old value and the release walk frees every counted register, so a
  register left holding a recycled frame's word would be released twice. And the
  registers the liveness analysis named -- the ones whose value can be observed
  before it is written, plus the scratch, window and handshake registers that sit
  outside the analysis domain -- must read `undefined`, because that is what the
  frame always presented.

  The existing code did the first property for free, by zeroing the whole
  register area (`all-bits-zero` is the integer 0: valid and uncounted), and then
  paid a scalar store loop for the second, writing `JS_UNDEFINED` into each named
  register. When there is no fill list -- a function read from a blob, whose side
  table is never serialized -- it filled *every* register with a scalar loop.

  The fill is on the JS-call path, so the loop's store count is the frame's
  register count, once per call.

  This fills the registers from a static block of `undefined` words instead:

      static const JSValue regvm_undef_tmpl[REGVM_UNDEF_TMPL_N] = {
          [0 ... REGVM_UNDEF_TMPL_N - 1] = { { .int32 = 0 }, JS_TAG_UNDEFINED },
      };

      if (likely(nregs <= REGVM_UNDEF_TMPL_N)) {
          memcpy(lay->regs, regvm_undef_tmpl, (size_t)nregs * sizeof(JSValue));
      } else if (!cb->regvm_fill) {
          ... existing scalar loop ...
      } else {
          ... existing zero-then-list fill ...
      }

  Filling all of them with `undefined` is a superset of what the analysis asks
  for and is still correct: `undefined` is valid and uncounted, so it satisfies
  the first property too, and the analysis's own list only ever *names* registers
  to set to `undefined`, never to any other value. Frames with more than
  `REGVM_UNDEF_TMPL_N` (256) registers keep the old paths; none of the built-in
  or measured programs reaches that, and 256 words is 4 KB of `.rodata`.

  The template is a constant initializer rather than a load-time constructor, so
  nothing has to run before `main`, and the fallback branch is a `likely` so the
  common path is a single `memcpy` with a length the caller already computed.

  Measured (`fixed.js`, 32 iterations, i7-8700): 23,834,989,409 ->
  23,600,642,543 instructions (**-0.234 G, -0.98 %**) and 11,088,407,289 ->
  11,159,266,968 cycles (flat within noise), against the plan's 0.33 G expected /
  0.2 G floor for this item. Gate run: 23,577,348,399 / 11,129,160,915.
  Checksum `546.1008391043414` exact; diff-suite `pass=398 fail=0 skip=0` mono and
  threaded; leak assertion clean; peak RSS 13240 KB (a 4 KB `.rodata` template).
  Re-measured on the landed `static const` build in an interleaved base+L1..L4
  session, the delta is unchanged within noise (23,840,570,326 -> 23,601,493,569,
  -0.239 G), confirming the `const` qualifier is codegen-neutral.

No opcode, operand encoding or serialized register-format change.
